{"id":"nautical","title":"Nautical","url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Nautical","rev":240599,"fetched":"2026-10-16","lead":[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"b","c":["Nautical interior"]}," design aesthetic is a classic architectural style that mimics the timeless, crisp atmosphere of coastal life and sea-faring ships. It is heavily characterized by a white and navy blue palette, prevalent use of weathered woods, crisp stripes, and authentic maritime artifacts. Unlike broader coastal styles that leans on generally on nautical, beach-like relaxation design specifically evokes a yacht-club, elegance or a rugged sailor's charm."]}],"sections":[{"title":"Visual","id":"visual","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["Nautical visuals mostly involve images of life on the sea, on a boat, ostructured,r even from the shore living in a lighthouse (which differentiates it from a ",{"t":"a","c":["Tropical"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Tropical"}," aesthetic, which tends to have more of a focus on warmer beaches as opposed to the rocky coasts often associated with Lighthouse imagery). This aesthetic also includes or relates to a ship tied up to the dock. This aesthetic gives the feeling of being at sea or on the ocean or relaxing on a boat or a yacht. Elements that can be included in the Nautical aesthetic include:"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["The ocean and ",{"t":"a","c":["beach"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Beach_Day"}]},{"c":["Boating/sailing"]},{"c":["Salty air"]},{"c":["Turtles"]},{"c":["Dolphins"]},{"c":["Seagulls"]},{"c":["Docks and boardwalks"]},{"c":["Lighthouses"]},{"c":["Beach houses"]}]}]},{"title":"Fashion","id":"fashion","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["Fashion found in the aesthetic often involves a navy jacket with brass buttons, a crisp white sailor's uniform, a sou'wester hat, and a yellow slicker, or a fisherman's sweater. Historic traditions in nautical dress continue to influence modern nautical apparel. When it comes to nautical dressing, blues, stripes, and sweaters are staples for a reason. Their look reflects the essence of what it should look and feel like to be on the sea. There is even a ",{"t":"a","c":["Lolita"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Lolita"}," subgenre based on sailors(as well as ",{"t":"a","c":["pirates"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Pirate"},") that can be worn. A lot of resort wear can also be included in Nautical fashion. Items, colors, and patterns tend to include:"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["Shades of blue, green, black, white, light pink, and cream colors"]},{"c":["Iridescence"]},{"c":["Scale patterns"]},{"c":["Loose fitting clothing"]},{"c":["Transparent and translucent materials"]},{"c":["Dresses"]},{"c":["Skirts"]},{"c":["Clothes featuring themes and motifs related to the sea"]},{"c":["Cardigans"]},{"c":["Beachwear"]}]}]},{"title":"Activities","id":"activities","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["This aesthetic brings out a calming lifestyle, so most of the time you can find yourself doing these activities:"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["Surfing"]},{"c":["Shopping locally"]},{"c":["Reading by the beach"]},{"c":["Boating"]},{"c":["Fishing"]},{"c":["Hanging out on a yacht"]}]}]},{"title":"Media","id":"media","blocks":[{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Movies"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Song of the Sea"]}," (2014)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Outer Banks"]}," (2020)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Moana"]}," (2016)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Life of Pi"]}," (2012)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Ponyo"]}," (2008)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["The SpongeBob SquarePants Movie"]}," (2004)"]}]},{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Music"]},{"t":"h","l":4,"c":["Albums"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Plastic Beach"]}," (2010) - Gorillaz"]},{"c":["Titanic Rising (2019) - Weyes Blood"]}]},{"t":"h","l":4,"c":["Music Artists"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["Cosmo Sheldrake"]}]},{"t":"h","l":4,"c":["Songs"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["The B-52's - \"Rock Lobster\""]}]},{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Video Games"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":